# Wave W17-AC (Route 228): storm post — a storm-fence marker post where the road gives out: a weathered post flying one small storm pennant at its head, red cloth snapped toward the desert — the fence’s own punctuation standing in the prop register (design: the storm fence at the north end marks where the charts give up; the posts stand where the road stops pretending). On wash turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the pennant entire: posts mark a road, this one marks its end.
